slice: 20 regions, 4 alignments
# Re-recorded 2026-10-18 (macOS host, arm64) when the built-in repeat-tract outlier weight went from 0.20 to 0.07 (parameters
# file format 6; src/calling/likelihood/ssr.rs DEFAULT_OUTLIER_WEIGHT). main d1b6e54f reproduced every old value on the same host
# first. Both parameters files move by two lines, format_version and the weight. Defaults route (5bfcecbf -> 916e114f): 453 of
# 7,509 records move, all STR, in QUAL; 10 sample genotypes change, 5 heterozygous to homozygous and 5 the reverse, so the 238
# heterozygous STR calls stay 238; no record appears or vanishes; no non-STR record moves. Fitted route (2cc2a44f -> e74465ad):
# 3 STR records appear (6,680 -> 6,683); 6 STR sample genotypes change (heterozygous STR calls 8 -> 14 of 1,720); one deletion
# overlapping a changed STR call moves a sample from 1/1 to 1/2, its second allele the spanning-deletion `*`; 1,574 non-STR
# records move only in PARALOG_LR / PARALOG_POST (by at most 0.00094 in posterior), because the hidden-duplication filter
# fits one rate over every record. They were 5bfcecbf / 6ab95191 / 954dd14f / 2cc2a44f.
# Re-recorded 2026-10-18 (macOS host, arm64) when a deletion touching a repeat tract's edge started counting as a flank
# deletion (str_edge_deletion_alleles.md §5.1, amended; doc/devel/reports/ng_str_edge_touching_2026-10-18.md). main 5c741b11
# reproduced every old value on the same host first. Defaults route (916e114f -> 9fc4a28f): 14 one-base generic deletions beside
# a tract leave as separate records and are written inside 14 widened STR records instead, mostly with the same genotypes; 3
# sample genotypes change (heterozygous to homozygous) where a tract's alleles re-split; 9 STR records move in QUAL; 1,305
# non-STR records move only in PARALOG_LR / PARALOG_POST (by at most 0.000045). The window lines move because the window table
# has one line per written record per sample: 12 new records a sample, and 7 near-tract records whose depth is counted over
# slightly different positions. The fitted file moves in 240 lines: reads with a flank deletion are left out of the stutter
# census (§5.3), so homopolymer slip rates at 16-21 repeats fall 15-24% (median row 0.5%). Fitted route (e74465ad -> 7aeeff78):
# 15 records only on the branch and 18 only on main, by the same swap; 3 sample genotypes change; 259 records move in QUAL.
# They were 916e114f / e1c72672 / b2fc1bfa / 8eb7fe42 / e74465ad.
# Re-recorded 2026-10-18 (macOS host, arm64) when the SNP/indel fit's census went from 128 chunks to 512
# (`CHUNKS_PER_CENSUS`; doc/devel/reports/reviews/perf_snp-fit_2026-10-18.md, finding L3), on top of the change above: the
# fit's sums are split at other positions, so its numbers move once, the same at every pool width (on the slice before this
# merge, the fitted file was identical at 4 and 18 threads). main 5490d1fb reproduced both old values on the same host first,
